  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nThe front has already departed the area and is expected to \nmeander through the Carolinas this weekend. Meanwhile, moisture \nlingering behind the front will sustain both cloud cover and at \nleast low-end chances of showers across the mountains and \nsouthern coalfields.\n\nAnother front sweeps across the area and propels the stalled front \nout to sea while the parent low travels through eastern Canada early \nnext week. Cooler and drier weather then sets in for the work week \nas high pressure builds in behind the secondary front.\n\nRadiational cooling under clear skies and calm flow will result in \nrather chilly nights, with potential for frost to develop in the \nnortheast mountains early Tuesday and Wednesday mornings. \nTemperatures then trend milder for the second half of the work\nweek.",
